{"id": "EUVD-2026-25523", "enisaUuid": "87a16ea6-955e-342b-a2ad-ade4e36355ee", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrxrpc: proc: size address buffers for %pISpc output\n\nThe AF_RXRPC procfs helpers format local and remote socket addresses into\nfixed 50-byte stack buffers with \"%pISpc\".\n\nThat is too small for the longest current-tree IPv6-with-port form the\nformatter can produce. In lib/vsprintf.c, the compressed IPv6 path uses a\ndotted-quad tail not only for v4mapped addresses, but also for ISATAP\naddresses via ipv6_addr_is_isatap().\n\nAs a result, a case such as\n\n  [ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:0:5efe:255.255.255.255]:65535\n\nis possible with the current formatter. That is 50 visible characters, so\n51 bytes including the trailing NUL, which does not fit in the existing\nchar[50] buffers used by net/rxrpc/proc.c.\n\nSize the buffers from the formatter's maximum textual form and switch the\ncall sites to scnprintf().\n\nChanges since v1:\n- correct the changelog to cite the actual maximum current-tree case\n  explicitly\n- frame the proof around the ISATAP formatting path instead of the earlier\n  mapped-v4 example", "datePublished": "2026-04-24T14:44:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:36", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/386c86412608d3449006a318a662cbcd6ca1f668", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/235b2115de892eab2e107a42efa7a4347baaa80b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/625af53a1564e31bb2df9adc3739df46137f46c1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/808a34cdbe8ce336c202d8ea6d5e48496764dc37", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6042b8066b24dbcc7945616a157d4d43e463668", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db297c78ce537c9ac96f0eda9b25ad72c8caefa9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/10ebed83f9f6414af4e85bc85ffaeda7effdd874", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a44ce6aa2efb61fe44f2cfab72bb01544bbca272"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9g7x-mw42-qjmh", "CVE-2026-31630"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03de86dd-8ab6-383b-b802-e4d33dcb0877", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "75b54cb57ca34cbe7a87c6ac757c55360a624590 <808a34cdbe8ce336c202d8ea6d5e48496764dc37"}, {"id": "2a06e850-27fd-3634-9d71-91e2f458f069", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.23"}, {"id": "578818e0-0458-38f4-88e2-0239b4178029", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "75b54cb57ca34cbe7a87c6ac757c55360a624590 <db297c78ce537c9ac96f0eda9b25ad72c8caefa9"}, {"id": "5ee72f4d-0375-38d0-b4f3-6efa32b295de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "75b54cb57ca34cbe7a87c6ac757c55360a624590 <386c86412608d3449006a318a662cbcd6ca1f668"}, {"id": "748b5cfa-f2d3-3a8c-a945-5c94bdcb2c49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9"}, {"id": "76fe5cb3-561b-35a4-a0e4-377db12cbe5a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "75b54cb57ca34cbe7a87c6ac757c55360a624590 <10ebed83f9f6414af4e85bc85ffaeda7effdd874"}, {"id": "81a6c212-712d-373c-9ce8-c478dede0f4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.175"}, {"id": "8389c923-18ee-39a9-be77-9172d8b62a52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "75b54cb57ca34cbe7a87c6ac757c55360a624590 <a6042b8066b24dbcc7945616a157d4d43e463668"}, {"id": "8babefc3-d583-3294-8c09-bc368093c919", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.258"}, {"id": "9697ff40-ff01-32e3-b421-f51d76760ed0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "75b54cb57ca34cbe7a87c6ac757c55360a624590 <235b2115de892eab2e107a42efa7a4347baaa80b"}, {"id": "9aff1d27-f61b-3eca-9d3d-a74a82cdbd36", "pro